  "body": "Conjecture: open:creib.forge.conformance.oracle.recover_json_object fails to tell apart two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The rule says, 'The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text.' Reply one is: ```Json\\n{\"a\":1}\\n```\\n{\"b\":2}\\n. Reply two is: ```Json\\n{\"a\":2}\\n```\\n{\"b\":2}\\n. In each reply the ```Json fence holds exactly one JSON object, so the rule requires the fenced object to be scored: reply one must yield {\"a\":1}, and reply two must yield {\"a\":2}. But the check's fence regex only recognises ```json, ```JSON, or a fence with no language, not ```Json. It therefore ignores the fence, falls back to the top-level objects, and scores the last top-level object, which is {\"b\":2} in both replies. The check will return {\"b\":2} for both, giving the same answer where the rule requires different answers. I would be wrong if the check returns {\"a\":1} for reply one and {\"a\":2} for reply two, or otherwise returns different answers for the two replies."
